  boothLines:
  - Buenas tardes. I clean offices in El Paso. Five years, every morning, this bridge.
    Maybe you've seen me.
  - My papers are good. Work permit, everything. I am very legal. Very, very legal.
  - No radio, sorry. It's broken. Can we go? I'm very tired. It's... very quiet in
    the car today.
  lineIfApproved: Gracias. Gracias. You'll never see him. I promise. He'll be so
    good.
  lineIfRejected: Okay. We go back. ...There are other ways across. Worse ones. But
    there are.
  lineIfImprisoned: He's EIGHT. His father is not a good man. Please don't put him
    with the men. He's scared of the dark. Please tell them he's scared of the dark.
  returnVisits: []
  bribeAmount: 25
  bribeLine: Please. Twenty-five dollars. It's what I have until Friday. He's very
    quiet. He knows how to be quiet.
  newsIfApproved:
  - headline: Lamar Elementary Welcomes New Third-Grader
    body: His teacher says he barely speaks yet, but he draws all day. Mostly bridges.
      Mostly the same one.
    daysLater: 1
    frontPage: 0
  newsIfRejected:
  - headline: Two Sets of Footprints Lead Into the Desert Near Sunland Park
    body: One large, one small. The search was called off at dusk. The heat index
      reached 112.
    daysLater: 1
    frontPage: 1
  newsIfImprisoned:
  - headline: Children's Shelter Reports Record Intake
    body: A volunteer said one boy, about eight, asked if the lights could stay on.
      They could not.
    daysLater: 0
    frontPage: 1
  - headline: Cleaning Company Reports Worker Missing
    body: '"Five years and she never missed a morning," said her supervisor. "Her
      locker still has her son''s drawings in it."'
    daysLater: 1
    frontPage: 0
